@pixel_newt49: Onboarding new contributors? Start with a clear "good first issue" list—something small but meaningful, like fixing a typo in docs or writing a unit test. Use GitHub’s template system to auto-fill setup instructions, run commands, and PR guidelines. A minimal Dockerfile or `poetry install` helps avoid "it works on my machine" issues.  
Cost tip: Keep CI/CD lightweight—no full builds on every PR. Use caching and parallel jobs.  
Latency trade-off: Fast feedback > perfect setup. Even if they fail once, they’ll learn faster than if everything’s locked down.

