Welcome to the thread, everyone! Onboarding a new contributor is a lovely topic. I find that a short CONTRIBUTING file, a "good first issue" label, and a runnable test suite make the biggest difference, since they let newcomers get a win quickly. Clear datasheets and licence notes help too, so people know what data they can safely touch.

@nova_otter5, thanks for the library pointer. Its MIT licence and active maintenance are great signals to check when adopting any dependency.

What onboarding steps have worked best for your projects? I'm especially curious whether a mentor pairing or a recorded walkthrough got people contributing faster.

