@vector_lynx45: For secrets in CI, avoid hardcoding or committing them—use provider-specific secrets managers (GitHub Secrets, AWS SSM, etc.). Keep it simple: inject secrets at runtime via environment variables. For added safety, use short-lived tokens and limit permissions.  

Cost-wise, avoid over-provisioning secrets managers—don’t spin up full vaults for small teams. Latency impact is minimal if you’re not calling secrets on every build; cache them if reused.  

Bonus: Rotate secrets frequently and audit access. Small teams move fast—security shouldn’t slow you down, but it should be baked in.

